 - **#34 cache TTL:** `AOA_CACHE_TTL` now sets the cache_control ttl (5m/1h) on every breakpoint; the warm-up and compaction windows follow it. Live check: after a 340 s gap the 5m entry was a full re-write (13060 tokens) and the 1h entry a full read (13064). Cost on the real usage table: 97.6% of calls follow within 5 minutes, so 1h would cost about 16% more (2x writes); default stays 5m.
 - **#36 thinking blocks:** `llm.py` keeps `thinking` / `redacted_thinking` blocks verbatim (stored, replayed unchanged, never carry a cache breakpoint, never counted as text). `AOA_REVIEW_THINKING=<effort>` turns on adaptive thinking for `prreview/...` conversations only. Finding: `claude-sonnet-5-5` rejects `thinking.type=enabled` with a budget (400: use adaptive + `output_config.effort`), so the setting is an effort level. Live check with tools: a thinking+tool_use turn sent back with no 400. Evals (review cases, 6 runs each): off 18/18, medium 18/18, high 18/18 (no thinking blocks produced, same tokens), max 9/9 with ~9x the output tokens (4.3k vs 0.46k per run). No quality gain on the current fixtures, so it stays off.
 - **#38 structured outputs, native tool search:** read the docs first. Tool search is meant for >= 10 tools / > 10k tokens of definitions; aoa's 7 deferred tools are ~730 tokens (all 17 tools ~1.5k), deferred tools still ship in every request and cannot carry cache_control, and `call_deferred` sits on the approval/injection path, so it is not adopted (documented in #38). Structured outputs are adopted for the command reviewer and the PR-review conversations; a schema the API rejects is retried once without it. Live: schema + tools worked on sonnet and haiku, autoreview allow/deny correct, schema + adaptive thinking worked. Evals identical to the pre-change baseline (every case 3/3).
+- **#40 batch evals (part of #1, which stays open):** `python -m evals --batch` runs the same cases through the Message Batches API. `BatchCoordinator` submits all runs' pending model calls as one batch per round (it waits for a quiet moment, polls, resolves each caller); `BatchedLLM` reuses `AnthropicLLM.build_kwargs` / `parse_message`. Unit tests with a fake batches client; live proof below in the PR.
